{%- comment -%}
  The two timestamps a status change writes.

  Nothing reads them yet, which is exactly why they are worth a test: by
  the time the service level work starts reading them, every ticket that
  has moved between now and then will carry whatever this wrote. A
  resolution time that is wrong is not recoverable after the fact.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  function s = 'modules/support/helpers/status/stamps', status: { "kind": "new" }
  function contract = 'modules/tests/assertions/equal', contract: contract, given: s.closed_at, expected: null, field_name: 'new stamps nothing'
  function contract = 'modules/tests/assertions/equal', contract: contract, given: s.solved_at, expected: null, field_name: 'new leaves solved_at alone'

  function s = 'modules/support/helpers/status/stamps', status: { "kind": "open" }
  function contract = 'modules/tests/assertions/equal', contract: contract, given: s.solved_at, expected: null, field_name: 'open stamps nothing'

  function s = 'modules/support/helpers/status/stamps', status: { "kind": "pending" }
  function contract = 'modules/tests/assertions/equal', contract: contract, given: s.solved_at, expected: null, field_name: 'pending stamps nothing'

  function s = 'modules/support/helpers/status/stamps', status: { "kind": "on_hold" }
  function contract = 'modules/tests/assertions/equal', contract: contract, given: s.solved_at, expected: null, field_name: 'on hold stamps nothing'

  comment
    Resolved is resolved and not closed. The seven day clock reads
    solved_at, and a closed_at here would stop it before it started.
  endcomment
  function s = 'modules/support/helpers/status/stamps', status: { "kind": "solved" }
  function contract = 'modules/tests/assertions/equal', contract: contract, given: s.closed_at, expected: null, field_name: 'solved is not closed'
  assign solved_stamped = false
  if s.solved_at != blank
    assign solved_stamped = true
  endif
  function contract = 'modules/tests/assertions/equal', contract: contract, given: solved_stamped, expected: true, field_name: 'solved stamps solved_at'

  comment
    Closing stamps both, because a ticket an agent closes outright was
    never marked resolved and still has a resolution time. The auto close
    is the exception and passes the original solved_at itself.
  endcomment
  function s = 'modules/support/helpers/status/stamps', status: { "kind": "closed" }
  assign both = false
  if s.closed_at != blank and s.solved_at != blank
    assign both = true
  endif
  function contract = 'modules/tests/assertions/equal', contract: contract, given: both, expected: true, field_name: 'closed stamps both'
  function contract = 'modules/tests/assertions/equal', contract: contract, given: s.closed_at, expected: s.solved_at, field_name: 'and stamps them with the same moment'
%}
